Hi all,

I ran across this figure and I thought it would be interesting as an interesting way to compare a multivariate data set. This is a plot describing some hockey statistics. However, I thought that it would interesting to apply this to the "iris" dataset. So for reference with a dummy set:

> iris[c(1,51,101),]
    Sepal.Length Sepal.Width Petal.Length Petal.Width    Species
1            5.1         3.5          1.4         0.2     setosa
51           7.0         3.2          4.7         1.4 versicolor
101          6.3         3.3          6.0         2.5  virginica

So in this example you'd divide the circle into four lines, then plot the suite of variables above with Species being the colour aesthetic connected by a line.

So my question is: Is this possible with ggplot2? Also but not specifically any input into this particular plot as a tool to visualize multivariate datasets. The thing that I like about this is that line pattern created should be a visual indication of similarity.

Thanks in advance.

Sam

