Hi,

Further to Tom's answer you can also do it with geom_polygon and coord_polar:

library(ggplot2)
library(reshape2)

pd <- iris[c(1, 51, 101),]
# express the values as a fraction of max value
pd[,1:4] <- apply(pd[,1:4], 2, function(x) x/max(x))
pd.melt <- melt(pd)
# duplicate the last entry to get the polygon to "join up"
pd.melt <- rbind(pd.melt, pd.melt[12,])

g <- ggplot(pd.melt, aes(x = variable, y = value, colour = Species, group = Species)) +
  coord_polar() +
  geom_polygon(fill = NA) +
  ylim(0, 1)

g

I see the point about these plots being misleading depending on the order of the `variable` factor. For better or worse I've also seen them 'sports analytics'.

Cheers,

(another) Tom

